Key the Darwin flags on the target alone

1.8.0 chose the Darwin link flags, the archive flags and the SDK's libc++
only when both the exec and the target platform were Darwin. A Linux host
targeting macOS then handed ld64.lld the ELF flags, which it refuses, and
compiled against the LLVM distribution's own libc++ headers, which lack
the __config_site a Darwin build needs. The object format and the C++
library follow the target, so all of it is keyed on the target.

1.8.0 also linked libtool, which those archive flags are for, on Darwin
hosts alone. Every LLVM release ships llvm-libtool-darwin, so every host
links it.

diff --git a/toolchain/cc_toolchain_config.bzl b/toolchain/cc_toolchain_config.bzl
